{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879694",
      "title": "What & Why?",
      "lectureOrder": 213,
      "videoOrder": 186,
      "sourceHash": "248caf8d235f90c218c79e0b94b2a8f90e5b580b57d9ea6041da402561357909",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.15,
          "end": 5.656,
          "en": "So, exactly is Vuex?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.656,
          "end": 10.5,
          "en": "Vuex is a library for managing global state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.5,
          "end": 12.78,
          "en": "Okay, that's a nice sentence.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.78,
          "end": 14.18,
          "en": "What does it mean?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.18,
          "end": 15.84,
          "en": "What's state?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.84,
          "end": 19.09,
          "en": "State could simply be translated with data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.09,
          "end": 23.85,
          "en": "data your application needs and data that affects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.85,
          "end": 26.53,
          "en": "what the user sees on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.53,
          "end": 30.56,
          "en": "So, you can think of state as reactive data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.56,
          "end": 34.45,
          "en": "data which may change and where such changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.45,
          "end": 37.63,
          "en": "then should trigger something on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.63,
          "end": 41.63,
          "en": "And Vue.js is all about this reactivity, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.63,
          "end": 43.59,
          "en": "as you learn throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.59,
          "end": 47.62,
          "en": "But managing data, state, that affects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.62,
          "end": 51.31,
          "en": "different components of your app can be tricky.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.31,
          "end": 52.94,
          "en": "For that it's important though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.94,
          "end": 56.74,
          "en": "to differentiate between two main kinds of state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.74,
          "end": 59.473,
          "en": "local state and global state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.67,
          "end": 64.83,
          "en": "Local state is the state the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.83,
          "end": 67.11,
          "en": "you manage inside of one component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.11,
          "end": 71.62,
          "en": "which only affects this one component and possibly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.62,
          "end": 75.59,
          "en": "indirectly through props, also a child component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.59,
          "end": 78.37,
          "en": "Here examples could be user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.37,
          "end": 81.94,
          "en": "that was entered into input elements, or for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.94,
          "end": 85.94,
          "en": "a button that shows or hides some container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.94,
          "end": 87.81,
          "en": "And I got an example for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.81,
          "end": 91.35,
          "en": "This is a course project we built a little bit earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.35,
          "end": 95.02000000000001,
          "en": "in the course after the main component sections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.02000000000001,
          "end": 97.34,
          "en": "It's this learning resource manager",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.78,
          "end": 102.47,
          "en": "and in there in the AddResource.Vue file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.47,
          "end": 105.94,
          "en": "in the AddResource component, we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.94,
          "end": 109.47999999999999,
          "en": "have a form where we fetch user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.47999999999999,
          "end": 113.95,
          "en": "And that user input, as well as the overall form validity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.95,
          "end": 116.21000000000001,
          "en": "only matters to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.21000000000001,
          "end": 120.72,
          "en": "Here for example we have this inputisInvalid data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.72,
          "end": 124.49,
          "en": "and therefore that would be the state of that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.49,
          "end": 129.49,
          "en": "which influences whether or not we show this dialogue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.89,
          "end": 135.59,
          "en": "So, this inputisInvalid data piece is state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.59,
          "end": 138.73,
          "en": "because it affects what the user sees on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 138.73,
          "end": 141.13,
          "en": "We show or don't show this dialogue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141.13,
          "end": 144.09,
          "en": "And it really only matters to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 144.09,
          "end": 147.05,
          "en": "We manage it internally in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.05,
          "end": 149.913,
          "en": "So, that would be an example for a local state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 150.87,
          "end": 155.417,
          "en": "On the other hand, global state is state data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.28,
          "end": 161.28,
          "en": "that affects multiple components, possibly the entire app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 161.8,
          "end": 165.06,
          "en": "So, data which you need in a lot of different places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.06,
          "end": 169.44,
          "en": "Examples here could be the user authentication status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 169.44,
          "end": 172.07,
          "en": "whether a user is logged in or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 172.07,
          "end": 174.85,
          "en": "shopping card items which might be presented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.85,
          "end": 179.47,
          "en": "in different parts of the app, and similar examples.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.47,
          "end": 181.79,
          "en": "Again, in this app I just showed you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.79,
          "end": 184.76,
          "en": "an example for a global state could be found",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 184.76,
          "end": 187.71,
          "en": "in the TheResources.vue file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 187.71,
          "end": 191.51,
          "en": "In there I got these stored resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 191.51,
          "end": 195.25,
          "en": "and those stored resources are changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 195.25,
          "end": 198.154,
          "en": "through the addResource method, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.154,
          "end": 200.79,
          "en": "but this method is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 200.79,
          "end": 204.57999999999998,
          "en": "from inside another component and the StoredResources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 204.57999999999998,
          "end": 208.02,
          "en": "are also used in other components of this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 208.02,
          "end": 212.313,
          "en": "So, this is an app wide, or at least a multicomponent state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 217.09,
          "en": "It's data that's used across multiple components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 217.09,
          "end": 221.57999999999998,
          "en": "And it's the global state where Vuex can help us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 221.57999999999998,
          "end": 223.4,
          "en": "Because thus far, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 223.4,
          "end": 225.61,
          "en": "in this app I just showed you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 225.61,
          "end": 230.61,
          "en": "we managed this state through provide and inject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 230.85,
          "end": 233.856,
          "en": "And this works, and this is not necessarily bad,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 233.856,
          "end": 236.6,
          "en": "but it has a couple of drawbacks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 236.6,
          "end": 239.52,
          "en": "which might or might not matter to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 239.52,
          "end": 242.67,
          "en": "One potential disadvantage for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.67,
          "end": 245.67,
          "en": "is that you end up with all the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 245.67,
          "end": 249.43,
          "en": "and all the methods to change the data in one component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 249.43,
          "end": 252.47,
          "en": "In this case, the TheResources component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 252.47,
          "end": 254.65,
          "en": "which therefore gets rather big",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 254.65,
          "end": 257.5,
          "en": "and which has a lot of data and a lot of methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 257.5,
          "end": 260.209,
          "en": "inside of it, which isn't really needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 260.209,
          "end": 262.44,
          "en": "for the template of that component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 262.44,
          "end": 265.79,
          "en": "but which is simply needed in other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 265.79,
          "end": 267.8,
          "en": "So, getting such a big component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 267.8,
          "end": 270.062,
          "en": "which manages cross components state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 270.062,
          "end": 274.54,
          "en": "that can be hard to maintain as your application grows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 274.54,
          "end": 276.47,
          "en": "and as you maybe have more and more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 276.47,
          "end": 278.053,
          "en": "global state to manage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.99,
          "end": 281.69,
          "en": "In addition, provide and inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 281.69,
          "end": 286.69,
          "en": "can have some tricky problems regarding reactivity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 286.79,
          "end": 290.08,
          "en": "It depends on which data you provide and inject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 290.08,
          "end": 292.21,
          "en": "And whilst there are solutions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 292.21,
          "end": 294.53,
          "en": "for all possible problems you could face,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294.53,
          "end": 298.723,
          "en": "a solution like Vuex in the end might be the best solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 299.64,
          "end": 303.01,
          "en": "Now, why exactly is Vuex a good solution though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 303.01,
          "end": 304.993,
          "en": "Why might it be worth a look?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 305.85,
          "end": 308.65,
          "en": "As I just outlined, managing app wide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 308.65,
          "end": 311.32,
          "en": "or global state can be difficult.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 311.32,
          "end": 313.86,
          "en": "You end up with such fat components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 313.86,
          "end": 315.65,
          "en": "which have a lot of logic in them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 315.65,
          "end": 318.49,
          "en": "which isn't needed for the component's template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 318.49,
          "end": 320.89,
          "en": "but in other components of the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 320.89,
          "end": 323.89,
          "en": "You also might have unpredictable behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 323.89,
          "end": 326.33,
          "en": "in your application because it's not always",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 326.33,
          "end": 330.14300000000003,
          "en": "immediately obvious where state gets changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 330.14300000000003,
          "end": 333.124,
          "en": "or maybe it's possible to change state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 333.124,
          "end": 336.57,
          "en": "in ways that you don't want it to be changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 336.57,
          "end": 340.01,
          "en": "It also could be error prone because accidental",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 340.01,
          "end": 343.46,
          "en": "or missed state updates could happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 343.46,
          "end": 347.04,
          "en": "Coming back to this example in the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 347.04,
          "end": 351.61,
          "en": "where we inject the resources, we get the resources array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 351.61,
          "end": 355.25,
          "en": "which we also manage in TheResources.vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 355.25,
          "end": 358.3,
          "en": "Now, theoretically, we could edit this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 358.3,
          "end": 360.7,
          "en": "in the place where it is injected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 360.7,
          "end": 364.92,
          "en": "and we would be editing the exact same array in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 364.92,
          "end": 368.53,
          "en": "We're not doing this here, but you could do it accidentally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 368.53,
          "end": 371.06,
          "en": "or maybe because a colleague is working on the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 371.06,
          "end": 372.783,
          "en": "who isn't paying close attention.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 373.68,
          "end": 375.7,
          "en": "And that is exactly what I mean with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 375.7,
          "end": 378.52,
          "en": "it being unpredictable or error prone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 378.52,
          "end": 380.8,
          "en": "You can edit data in places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 380.8,
          "end": 382.87,
          "en": "where it shouldn't really be edited.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 382.87,
          "end": 384.29,
          "en": "Of course, if you're working on your own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 384.29,
          "end": 385.62,
          "en": "this might not be a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 385.62,
          "end": 387.89,
          "en": "but in bigger projects and in bigger teams,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 387.89,
          "end": 389.253,
          "en": "it could become a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 390.12,
          "end": 392.53,
          "en": "And that's exactly where Vuex helps us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 392.53,
          "end": 397.53,
          "en": "because with Vuex, we outsource the state management.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 397.65999999999997,
          "end": 400.46,
          "en": "It's no longer in such fat components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 400.46,
          "end": 402.61,
          "en": "instead it's in a separate place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 402.61,
          "end": 404.83299999999997,
          "en": "detached from the components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 405.84000000000003,
          "end": 408.68399999999997,
          "en": "It's also a more predictable because Vuex has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 408.68399999999997,
          "end": 412.87,
          "en": "some clear rules on where state should be managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 412.87,
          "end": 415.76,
          "en": "and how it should be updated and shared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 415.76,
          "end": 418.61,
          "en": "And therefore it's also less error prone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 418.61,
          "end": 421.51,
          "en": "because we have that clearly defined data flow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 421.51,
          "end": 423.68,
          "en": "which we have to adhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 423.68,
          "end": 425.92,
          "en": "So, that's the what and why.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 425.92,
          "end": 429.963,
          "en": "Now let's install Vuex and let's get started using it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
